<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6536"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 5:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Snuff, not a bad theory. Even if he filmed on old super 8, the films could go for alot of money. Fits the photography angle too. Snuff films are hard to track tho arnt they? If it is snuff and he is selling it, who then are the buyers? There must be a ring of some sort. But then why did he stop for so long. Did he pack up shop and go to Mexico? Could be possible. Could explain his &#34;accent&#34; or cover up with fake accent. Snuff films are made alot in Mexico I&#39;ve heard. Wasn&#39;t there also a movie about snuff films. Nicolas Cage. Wasn&#39;t that in Mexico?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
