<!--Post: 6538--><!--Time: 1107871966-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6538"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 6:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not sure about the actual existance of any to date. They have a lot of staged ones, but last I heard the FBI said they have never turned up a real one. Thats not to say they don&#39;t exist. <BR> <BR>The child porn rings that I&#39;ve heard about being busted are international. In my opinion, if this theory holds water, Josephine was the intended victim, and this is very hard core child porn. <BR> <BR>Tracing the film would be next to impossible, however the FBI would start hammering away at the local porn, child porn, and particularly the prostitution ring that was popped in Wichita and OKC and Texas to Mexico in the last couple of weeks. Networks overlap and someone will want to deal out of kidnapping and possibly child porn considering the age of the girls. <BR> <BR>Then they confiscate computers and check email and other tracks pointing to sources.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not saying that BTK or his tapes are well known, but only someone wealthy could afford the price. Considering the crime, there will be a lot of roll overs and deals to be cut. They just need to find one customer and say the words &#39;wittness protection&#39;, and that&#39;s that. <BR> <BR>Of course I could be totally wrong, but I have yet to find a hitch in the case that can&#39;t be explained by a &#39;money motive&#39;rather than an inconsistant head case. <BR> <BR>Why&#39;d he quit? He got rich. Why work or take chances.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6538-->
<!--Post: 6548--><!--Time: 1107884385-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6548"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 9:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BModule: <BR> <BR>A most interesting possibility.   <BR> <BR>The only thing I question is the part about BTK taking chances.  While he supposedly quit killing, it seems &#40;to me&#41; that he is still taking chances by taunting the police.   <BR> <BR>If he made his porn/tape money and got away with it -- he should simply just shut up and stop taunting the police. <BR> <BR>He might otherwise have been presumed dead if he just kept quiet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
